<title>FINLAND: FINNLINES FLAGS OWNERSHIP CHANGE.</title>
<headline>FINNLINES FLAGS OWNERSHIP CHANGE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish cargo shipping company Finnlines Oy said in a statement on Thursday that the combined stake of Veikko Laine Oy, Laatusailyke Oy and Pentti Laine had risen over 10 percent, to 10.7 percent of shares and votes.</p>
<p>It said their holdings totalled 2.05 million shares.</p>
<p>In its 1996 annual report, Finnlines said Veikko Laine Oy owned 1.47 million shares or 7.64 percent at the end of the year while Laatusailyke Oy owned 0.39 million shares or 2.03 percent.</p>
<p>The annual report did not list Pentti Laine among Finnlines' 10 biggest owners at end-1996.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
